# What must NOT enter the image, and why.
#
# The repository is roughly 4 GB on disk and the useful image is around 1 GB. Almost the whole
# difference is generated data that the service never opens. Without this file `COPY . .` ships all of
# it, and the build is slow, the push is slow, and every deployment pays for it.

# ---- toolchains: rebuilt inside the image, never copied ---------------------------------
.venv
.node
ui/node_modules
ui/.next
ui/out
ui/reports
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.git
.gitignore
.DS_Store

# `ui/out` is excluded on purpose even though it is committed. Stage 1 rebuilds it from source, so
# copying the committed one in would risk shipping a stale export that silently disagrees with the
# records in the same image.
# `ui/reports` is the staging copy the build reads; stage 1 recreates it from `reports/`.

# ---- generated data: excluded, with ONE exception --------------------------------------
# The event stream is ~1.1 GB and the fusion component caches are ~216 MB each. Both regenerate from
# committed configuration and the service never reads either, so they stay out.
#
# The model directory holds EIGHT bundles totalling ~628 MB, and the service loads exactly one of them:
# the issuer view for the issuer-side persona. Shipping the other seven would add half a gigabyte to
# serve requests nothing makes, because the interface only ever asks for the issuer view.
#
# The `.prefusion-g1_only` bundles are excluded twice over, and that is deliberate: they carry the
# defective fusion weights measured at 0.0842 against 0.3515 for the corrected combiner. An image that
# could load one would silently serve scores four times worse than everything reported.
#
# To serve another deployment position, add its bundle here explicitly. Do not widen this to a glob:
# `gate-i_*` also matches `gate-i_issuer.prefusion-g1_only`.
data/**
!data/models/gate-i_issuer/**

# ---- documentation and logs -------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
deploy/
docs/
tests/
